course: dictionary
lesson: 12750
title: Dumplings: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it: they are its context. «We had beef stew and dumplings for supper.» The clues stew and supper tell you dumplings are food cooked in a pot.
explain: «My nan folds dumplings with her fingers and steams them until they are soft.» Folds and steams are clues that dumplings here are little parcels of dough with a filling inside. Always test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with «dumpling» used as a name: «Grandma called the baby her little dumpling.» A baby is not a meal, so this is a fond pet name for a small, chubby child. The loving feeling in the sentence is another clue.
fact: Dumplings are small balls of dough cooked in boiling water, soup or stew.
fact: Dumplings can also be little parcels of thin dough with a filling of meat, vegetables or fruit, steamed, boiled or fried.
fact: Chinese jiaozi, Polish pierogi and Ukrainian varenyky are all kinds of dumplings.
fact: «Steamed dumplings» and «apple dumplings» are common phrases about food.
fact: Informally, «dumpling» is a fond pet name for a small, chubby child.
exercise: «We had beef stew and dumplings for supper.» What are the dumplings here? | Pieces of fruit dropped in a pond | Small, chubby children | A kind of shoe | *Small balls of dough cooked in soup or stew
exercise: «Lin's family ate jiaozi, which are dumplings filled with meat and vegetables.» Which meaning fits best? | *Little parcels of thin dough with a filling | A pet name for a baby | Stones used to build a wall | Long, thin noodles
exercise: Grandma smiles and says, «Our little dumpling is finally asleep.» What does dumpling mean? | *A fond pet name for a small, chubby child | A parcel of dough | A bowl of hot soup | A kind of cake
test: Pierogi, varenyky and kreplach are all types of what? | Clouds | Pencils | *Dumplings | Bicycles
test: «Mum said, I will steam the apple dumplings for pudding.» What are the apple dumplings? | A wooden spoon | *A sweet dough parcel with apple inside | A pile of leaves | A pet name for a child
exam: Which sentence uses dumpling as a pet name? | *Grandad hugged his little dumpling and laughed. | The soup was hot and dumplings floated in it. | Dad made dumplings with the leftover dough. | We steamed dumplings for Lunar New Year.
